      },
      "set_b": {
        "source": ["host", "link:Structural"],
        "categories": [
          "OST_StructuralFraming", "OST_StructuralColumns", "OST_StructuralFoundation"
        ]
      },
      "default_assignee": "Mechanical"
    },
    {
      "id": "default-mep-soft-clearance",
      "name": "MEP Soft Clearance",
      "kind": "soft",
      "tolerance_inches": 1.0,
      "set_a": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": [
          "OST_DuctCurves", "OST_DuctFitting", "OST_DuctAccessory", "OST_FlexDuctCurves",
          "OST_PipeCurves", "OST_PipeFitting", "OST_PipeAccessory", "OST_FlexPipeCurves",
          "OST_Sprinklers",
          "OST_Conduit", "OST_ConduitFitting", "OST_CableTray", "OST_CableTrayFitting"
        ]
      },
      "set_b": {
        "source": ["host", "link:Architectural", "link:Structural"],
        "categories": [
          "OST_Walls", "OST_Floors", "OST_Ceilings",
          "OST_StructuralFraming", "OST_StructuralColumns"
        ]
      },
      "default_assignee": "Mechanical"
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Phase 4 clearance tests. kind=clearance rows are code-zone violations, not element-vs-element hits: set_b is the OWNER (the gear the zone belongs to), set_a is the INTRUDER. The test id IS the scoring discriminator (clearance_rule) -- the ids C-NEC / C-NEC-W / M-NEC-PROT / M-SPR must stay exactly as written.",
      "id": "C-NEC",
      "name": "NEC 110.26 Dedicated Space",
      "kind": "clearance",
      "tolerance_inches": 0.0,
      "set_a": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": [
          "OST_DuctCurves", "OST_DuctFitting", "OST_DuctAccessory", "OST_FlexDuctCurves",
          "OST_PipeCurves", "OST_PipeFitting", "OST_PipeAccessory", "OST_FlexPipeCurves",
          "OST_MechanicalEquipment"
        ]
      },
      "set_b": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": ["OST_ElectricalEquipment"]
      },
      "default_assignee": "Electrical"
    },
    {
      "$comment": "set_a is MEP obstructions only (no OST_Walls): the actionable C-NEC-W violation is a duct/pipe/conduit routed through a panel's working space. Walls were dropped (V4 deep dive) -- recessed-panel bounding boxes caught the electrical-room's own boundary walls, producing ~100 non-actionable false flags, and a wall in the working space is an architectural room-sizing issue, not an MEP reroute.",
      "id": "C-NEC-W",
      "name": "NEC 110.26 Working Space",
      "kind": "clearance",
      "tolerance_inches": 0.0,
      "set_a": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": [
          "OST_DuctCurves", "OST_DuctFitting", "OST_FlexDuctCurves",
          "OST_PipeCurves", "OST_PipeFitting", "OST_FlexPipeCurves",
          "OST_Conduit", "OST_ConduitFitting", "OST_CableTray", "OST_CableTrayFitting",
          "OST_MechanicalEquipment", "OST_PlumbingFixtures"
        ]
      },
      "set_b": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": ["OST_ElectricalEquipment"]
      },
      "default_assignee": "Electrical"
    },
    {
      "id": "M-NEC-PROT",
      "name": "NEC 110.26(E)(1)(b) Foreign Systems Above",
      "kind": "clearance",
      "tolerance_inches": 0.0,
      "set_a": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": [
          "OST_PipeCurves", "OST_PipeFitting", "OST_PipeAccessory", "OST_FlexPipeCurves",
          "OST_Sprinklers"
        ]
      },
      "set_b": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": ["OST_ElectricalEquipment"]
      },
      "default_assignee": "Electrical"
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Dormant on models with no modeled sprinkler heads (set_b resolves to zero); the runner reports skipped_reason no_owner_elements and does not flag it a suspect test.",
      "id": "M-SPR",
      "name": "NFPA 13 Sprinkler Obstruction",
      "kind": "clearance",
      "tolerance_inches": 0.0,
      "set_a": {
        "source": ["host", "link:Structural"],
        "categories": [
          "OST_DuctCurves", "OST_DuctFitting", "OST_FlexDuctCurves",
          "OST_PipeCurves", "OST_PipeFitting",
          "OST_Conduit", "OST_CableTray",
          "OST_MechanicalEquipment", "OST_StructuralFraming"
        ]
      },
      "set_b": {
        "source": "host",
        "categories": ["OST_Sprinklers"]
      },
      "default_assignee": "Fire Protection"
    }
  ]
}
